  'cli.usage':
    'Usage: inlaycms <command> [options]\n\nCommands:\n  serve    Run the site and the admin from the data folder set in INLAY_DATA_DIR (the other settings are INLAY_ environment variables)\n  dev [--config <file>] [--port <n>]\n           Run the site from its source on this computer (default port 3000), restarting it when a file changes; its data goes in a data folder next to the config file\n  push <host> [--file <file>] [--activate] [--dry-run] [--name <name>] [--token <token>] [--key <file>] [--no-typecheck] [--insecure]\n           Send a release to the server at <host> (an http:// or https:// address) and print what it changes: the site is packed first unless --file names a release file\n  activate <host> <id> [--token <token>] [--insecure]\n           Make a release on the server at <host> live, also to go back to an earlier one\n  activate <file-or-id> [--data <dir>] [--name <name>] [--server-stopped]\n           Make a release live while the server is stopped: a release file is stored first, an ID names a stored release\n  releases <host> [--token <token>] [--json] [--insecure]\n           List the releases on the server at <host>\n  releases [--data <dir>] [--json]\n           List the releases in the server\'s data folder\n  check    Check the database updates and starting content the site code needs, without changing anything\n           With --export <file>, check an export file instead\n  backup   Write a backup archive of the database and media\n  export [--out <file>]\n           Write all content and media to an export archive (default: inlay-export-<time>.tar.gz)\n  import <file> [--dry-run] [--server-stopped]\n           Replace the content with an export; --dry-run only reports what would happen\n  restore-backup <file> [--server-stopped]\n           Replace the database and media with a backup, and the live release with the one in it (the server must be stopped)\n  create-owner --email <email> --name <name>\n           Create the owner of the site; the password is read from the terminal or stdin\n  create-token --email <email> --name <name> [--push]\n           Make an API key for a user and print it, only this once; with --push, a push token for inlaycms push (owners only)\n  reset-password --email <email>\n           Set a new password for a user, for when they are locked out; the password is read from the terminal or stdin. They are signed out everywhere and their API keys stop working\n  keygen [--out <dir>] [--name <name>]\n           Make a key pair for signing releases (default: inlay.key and inlay.pub in the current directory)\n  pack [--key <file>] [--out <file>] [--name <name>] [--no-typecheck]\n           Make a signed release file of the site (default: <name>.tgz in the current directory)\n\nOptions:\n  --config <file>      Config file (default: inlay.config.ts, .js or .mjs in the current directory)\n  --port <n>           dev only: the port to run the site on (default: INLAY_PORT or 3000)\n  --db <file>          The database file, instead of the one in the config file\n  --data <dir>         The data folder of a host, instead of INLAY_DATA_DIR: activate and releases without a <host> always use one; backup, export, import, restore-backup, create-owner, create-token and reset-password use it instead of a config file (and use INLAY_DATA_DIR when there is no config file)\n  --token <token>      push, and activate and releases with a <host>: the push token (default: INLAY_PUSH_TOKEN)\n  --insecure           push, and activate and releases with a <host>: allow an http:// address that isn\'t this computer\n  --file <file>        push only: send this release file instead of packing the site\n  --activate           push only: make the release live once the server has it (not with --dry-run)\n  --export <file>      check only: check this export file instead of the database\n  --out <path>         export and pack: where to write the file; keygen: the folder for the keys\n  --name <name>        create-owner: the owner name; create-token: the key name; keygen: the key file name (default: inlay); pack, push and activate: the release name\n  --key <file>         pack and push: the private key to sign with (default: INLAY_SIGNING_KEY, the key itself or a path to it)\n  --no-typecheck       pack and push: skip the type check of the site code\n  --push               create-token only: let the key push and make releases live\n  --dry-run            import: report what would be restored, change nothing; push: report what the release would change, keep nothing\n  --server-stopped     import, restore-backup and activate: go ahead even though the database looks in use\n  --json               check, import --dry-run and releases: print the report as JSON\n  --help               Show this help',
