  'mcp.tool.describe_site.title': 'Describe the site',
  'mcp.tool.describe_site.description':
    "Shows the site's languages, its pages (singletons), its shared content (globals) and its collections, with their ids, addresses and help from the developer, the name of the release the site runs, and how many pages and entries of each type are missing something the site now requires (see list_gaps). Start here.",
  'mcp.tool.describe_type.title': 'Describe a content type',
  'mcp.tool.describe_type.description':
    "Shows the fields and parts of a content type, with each field's label and help, and the JSON Schema its content follows. Read it before creating or changing content of this type.",
  'mcp.tool.get_document.title': 'Read a page or entry',
  'mcp.tool.get_document.description':
    'Reads one page, entry or global in one language: its content (in the form update_document and create_entry accept), its ids, its address on the live site (null until it is published there) and a preview link. Give its id, or its type (and slug, for an entry of a collection whose entries have pages).',
  'mcp.tool.search_entries.title': 'Find entries',
  'mcp.tool.search_entries.description':
    'Finds entries of a collection whose title or text contains every word of the query, ignoring case and accents. Leave out the query to list the newest entries.',
  'mcp.tool.list_gaps.title': 'List missing content',
  'mcp.tool.list_gaps.description':
    "Lists the pages and entries whose published version is missing something the site now requires, such as a required field added after they were published, with each missing field, and how many there are in all. Visitors still see them as they are. Fill in the fields with update_document, then publish. Give a type to list only that type. Returns 50 at a time by default; use offset to see the next ones.",
  'mcp.param.type': 'The content type, as named in describe_site.',
  'mcp.param.gapType': 'Only list pages and entries of this content type, as named in describe_site.',
  'mcp.param.gapsLimit': 'How many pages and entries to return, at most 100. Defaults to 50.',
